Abomination: It was possibly once human but is now just a disgusting thing. These weird creatures are hosts to a local species of rot loving flies. They drip green stinky goo everywhere they walk and spit disgusting liquid with every movement of their mouth.
DecayFly: A species of fly that loves the decay of the Corruption, they often nest inside of living creatures.
BabyGlowmarin: These small adorable fish are from another dimension, they reproduce really fast. Its small glow organs are already developed and work fine.
Gilania: Big reptiles that live in the desert, their bite is venomous. They will rest underground at day to escape the blazing desert sun and come out at night.
SandEle: They are actually crystalized mana surrounded by sand, created artificially by a cult. They will react hostile against anything that enters their desert. During sandstorms they become even more active and travel to the surface, sometimes following Sand Elementals.
Darkling: An entity that was created from Void Matter, they curiously approach people who pass by in the dungeon and only attack when threatened.
Ashton: A weird creature that roams the frozen section of the underworld, hovering as if hanging on strings. They spit burning cold ash at everything that doesn't belong.
SearedAshton: A subspecies of Ashton that adapted to live in the seething heat of the underworld, they spit hot burning ash clouds.
IceDrakeJuvenile: Juvenile Ice Drakes usually reside underground where they hunt prey via ambush. They can be approached savely when they are asleep. They really love gilded dishes.
Glowmarin: A fish from another dimension, they have glowing organs all over their body, suggesting that they originally lived in deeper waters.
Lobster: Odd lobster species that lives near the shores, they have a parrot like beak which gives them their name. Their meat is very tasty and can make a nice dish.
StormEel: The great storm eels, only active during storms, when the sea is harsh and unforgiving. Many people believe they are scouts of something deep under the ocean. That is why these creatures are seen as an omen of even worse to come.
Dusty: Piles of cooled ash given life by the potent magic of the Frozen Underworld. They have no mind or soul, they only fly around on the icy winds, exploding into ash on impact.
Victim: A poor soul that has lost everything to the burning winds of ice. They fled through a space-time rift into the Underworld after their home had begun to slowly be consumed by the Abyssal Sin. They have long forgotten who they even are.
VictimEye: The eye of a Victim, it became sentient after its host body started to show signs of weakness.
IceDemon: A demon that has managed to adapt to the icy winds of the Frozen Underworld. They utelize powerful magic spears but... there must be something slumbering deep within.
Madman: A simple man who witnessed the true horror, no longer able to think like a normal person.
MadnessFlier: A flying entity that mutated into a grotesque something, just touching its skin hurts mentally.
MadnessGazer: A giant eyeball creature that flies by flapping its grotesque tentacles around. They might have been the eye of an unfortunate soul that witnessed the horrors.
MadnessStarving: A gruesome creature that gazed into the lurking terror, its madness scarred mind cannot properly comprehend the process of consumption anymore, leaving it in a terrible state, craving for food but not being able to die either.
MadTitan: A bulky creature that follows the horrors, its soul has been empowered by the madness energy inside it. It possesses an arm cannon with which it can fire massive amounts of madness, maybe suggesting that it might have been a normal gun at some point that fused with its holder.
PetDrake: Ice Drakes were normally very docile creatures, often enough even interacting with humans by themself. Though the war against the Vikings has left them scarred, now barely trusting anyone. Who knows, maybe some day, we can live in harmony again.
Admin: The creator and administrator of this world's frame, he was brought here with your help.
Taraha: A dimensional traveler who loves to trade items. "Find something here, trade somewhere else", that is her slogan.
Dappercap: The Mushroom Monarch's son, really nobody knows how in the world this works but here he is. He is up to mischief, hates everything he doesn't see as "cool" and even deals with illegal mushrooms. Maybe if you act cool enough, he will share them with you too.
Adel: Originating from a neighboring kingdom, this hallowed warrior wishes to avenge his beloved lord. He wields the Lightstream Mythos with which he has slain many foes. He was the first to declare war against Baaruun, against his new lord's will.
Vertrarius: A grumpy demon who wields the Evil Ember, Vulkanus. He is lazy and does not care about anyone but his lord, making him the most unreliable person in existence. When Gunresat declared war against Baaruun, he fought as Baaruun's leader out of boredom.
Smiley: The leader of the Darklings that hide inside the dungeon. His powers are unrivaled and respected amongst his followers and he is equally loved as well. In response to the incredible anger against his origins, his body turned pale to rebel against his darkness.
Grudge: The incarnation of despair and hope that piled up in the Frozen Underworld, born from the deep wishes of its residents and the abyssal magic that lurks inside. You have slain their biggest hope, so be assured, the winds are not happy about your slaughter.
MushroomMonarch: A royal mushroom who rests in the Scarlet Mycelium Forest. He had more light to fight with a long time ago, but it has since faded. Nowadays he is just a grumpy old king in his tiny kingdom of peace.
RedMushling: The monarchs loyal servants which are formed from his own flesh. They have no mind, only following their task to kill whatever is in their way.
FeudalFungus: A large humanoid glowing mushroom who is known as the glowing royalty. As its name suggests, it possesses an elegant blue hued glow that only becomes stronger the more it taps into its inner light. A long time ago it took upon the name "Umos", referencing the memory it now shares. Only the mushrooms know what hides under its light.
Toad: Rare toads that have grown large and somehow found their way into the glowing caverns. Their ability to jump is greatly crippled due to mycelium restraining the movement of their back legs. They are peaceful until provoked.
ShroomJelly: A jellyfish like creature who likes to hide buried in the ground disguised as a mushroom.
MyceliBug: Large insect that lives in the Scarlet Mycelium Forest, they feast on nutrients inside the mushrooms. They are harmless and simply sit beside travelers to observe them unless provoked.
MyceliLarva: Small larva who will eventually grow into a Myceli Bug. Just like their adult counterparts, they consume mushroom nutrients.
CapBunny: Unique bunny species who have evolved to live in harmony in the Scarlet Mycelium Forest.
Puffer: These large reptiles waddle through the Scarlet Mycelium Forest in search of only the best fungi to consume. If anything threatening looking draws too close, they will enter an alerted stance and release large spore clouds from their tail end. Their thick hide makes them extremely resistant against any attack.
Hovercap: Red mushrooms that are extremely lightweight with the ability to ride on even the smallest breeze. Just a slight disruption to their swift movement makes them crash down back to earth.
GripHot: This mysterious blazing hand stalks the night in search of something. Its skin seems to be made of a thin layer of flexible hardened volcanic ash, magma and flames are hiding inside.
GripWet: Mysterious floating hand that seems to be looking for something. Its thin skin layer consists of mud and biomatter, murky water can be found within.
Darkdrifter: Seahorse-like creatures that slowly drift around in the lake depths in groups.
SkySlug: Fascinating slugs that evolved wings to soar through the skies. A truly perfect majestic slimy flawless being whose beauty rivals those of the gods.
Skulker: Crabs that dwell in the moonlit marshes of the Shrouded Mire. They are extremely territorial and will attack anyone who comes too close to their nest. If defensive measures are required, be aware of their shells, as they can reflect incoming bullets.
BogFrog: This little friend is a relative of the jungle frogs, although darker in coloration. The Bog Frog prefers the dark and murky atmosphere of the Shrouded Mire over the humid jungle.
MoonMorpho: A peculiar butterfly that seems to enjoy the veil of the night. Its wings glow in a bright blue, serving as beacons in the misty bogs.
Newt: Lizards with dark coloration that dwell in the shrouded mire. They have bright green sacks on the sides and underside of their heads that can be used to discharge corrosive acid.
Miresquito: Giant bugs with a lust for blood. They relentlessly chase whatever looks large enough to satiate their hunger.
FogAngler: Male anglers that swim around in the shrouded mire and its depths. They hunt prey using their lures to deliver it to the females.
DepthAngler: Female Fog Anglers who exclusively live in the lake depths. Unlike their male counterpart, these fish are larger and mostly sit still on the floor. They keep waiting for an unfortunate creature to come too close, only to be swallowed whole.
MushSlime: A slime that has lived within the Scarlet Mycelium Forest for a good while. Mushrooms have grown inside, forming a large cap ontop. Mushroom Slimes can expell a cloud of spores when threatened.
MushroomPreacher: A mushroom given life by Umos the Feudal Fungus. They attempt to spread the words of the Light across the caverns, just as their glowing royalty did.
MushroomFollower: A sentient mushroom that follows the words of Light, seeking enlightenment. They will be often seen accompanying preachers.
AMindFromBeyond: Massive living brains that empower other maddened beings with a cerebral aura.
LilTerror: Bats with dark coloration that have evolved from Cave Bats to survive in the lake depths. Their claws contain a paralyzing venom.
Finfly: These bean shaped guys are an evolutionary offbranch of the Biofeeder. They flap their fins in such a high frequency that they look like underwater flies.
Biofeeder: Aquatic maggot like animal that sticks to walls in the lake depths to feed on washed up biomatter.
Mossling: Small younglings that cover themselves in moss to avoid detection from other predators. They are curious and playful, causing them to just ram into things for fun.
Mosster: These hulking monsters roam the Shrouded Mire as one of its apex predators. With its giant arms and claws, it tears apart prey with ease. They are very social, and tend to their young until adulthood
Stalker: Strange plant like creatures that dwell in foggy bogs. Unlike most other creatures native to the Shrouded Mire, these tend to disappear during nighttime.
Bloatleech: Large rotund leeches that have their home in the lake depths. With their sharp teeth, they dig into flesh to create big wounds to feed on.
Lecharvis: Wriggly bloatleech larvae that live in the lake depths. Due to their teeth not being developed yet, they rely on fresh blood their parents release from their caught prey.
Gaster: Interesting. VERY interesting. I have no damn clue where the hell I am right now. But it's dark, rather dark, yet perhaps even darkerer. Maybe I should not have taken that weird route to this rather dark world.

VanillaBestiaryEdits: {
	EyeofCthulhu: A massive flying eye, said to belong to a slain deity. Its origins lie in the lands of crimson flesh. Just another abomination born from a dying will.
	EaterofWorlds: A massive worm who is responsible for the many large chasms in the Corruption. It will devour all in its path in order to satisfy its hunger.
	BrainofCthulhu: The source of all crimson, a flying mastermind bereft of its former being. The brain has rotted beyond belief.
	Skeletron: The results of a necromantic experiment created deep within the Dungeon. Equipped with a sturdy curse, this tyrant guards the entrance to its home at all cost.
	WallofFlesh: This gigantic mass of flesh is the combined effort of thousands of demons who had to give their life to it. It houses the souls of many warriors who were locked away to end a war.
	Spazmatism: Needs lore rewrite first
	Retinazer: Needs lore rewrite first
	Destroyer: Needs lore rewrite first
	SkeletronPrime: Needs lore rewrite first
	Plantera: Filled with an artificial soul, this floral guardian wanders the jungle caverns with its only task in hand. It violently attacks those who hurt its offspring and the jungle they inhabit.
	EmpressofLight: The former guardian angel of the kingdom of Gunresat. She served in a rebellious army, but with her former masters gone, she moved on to follow goals of her own.
	MoonLord: The Moon Lord is but a husk, an unfinished shell to house Cthulhu's lost soul. Allowing this being to continue existing would spell certain doom for all life.
	Wyvern: Large draconic creatures that rule the skies of Veteravit as their apex predator. The release of the ancient spirits have agitated them greatly. They seem more powerful above other continents.
	Wraith: Souls belonging to the darkest of hearts, brought back into our world as evil shadows. Their malice stems from their forced pull into the mortal realm.
	WorldFeeder: Devourers that evolved due to excessive demon soul energy being released. They are destined to grow into an Eater of Worlds if not disposed of.
	Paladin: In distant history, these mighty undead knights once guarded the great kingdom of Librias before a massive curse befell them.
	ChaosElemental: Once warriors from the kingdom of Gunresat, they erratically make chase with an uncontrollable surge of luminous power.
	VoodooDemon: Higher ranking demons can possess a voodoo doll they shape into whatever they like. For some reason they collectively seem to love modeling the Guide.
	UndeadViking: Vikings who lost their lives during their war against the drakes, now reanimated, forced to roam the icy caverns.
	Harpy: Winged, demi-human women defend their territory against invaders by impaling them with their razor-sharp feathers. They originate from the Nimbaes Plateau hovering over the eastern continent.
	TacticalSkeleton: A skeleton equipped with firearms built by the mechanic. With thick armor and mighty boomsticks, it's clear these bones are prepared for a siege
	SkeletonCommando: A skeleton equipped with firearms built by the mechanic. Rocket-powered and fueled with rage, these cursed skeletons prefer the nuclear option.
	SkeletonSniper: A skeleton equipped with firearms built by the mechanic. These eagle-eyed sharpshooters let nothing escape their crosshairs.
	Demolitionist: An explosives revering dwarf from overseas. He honed his skills with explosives for a few years in the Steal Realm of Itorum, as it has only the most quality gunpowder.
	GoblinTinkerer: This goblin was exiled from the rest of his clan for being an intelligent pacifist. He attempted to hone his skills in gear augmenting in the outskirts of Itorum, but ended up breaking many an armament. Instead of not taking payment for these mistakes, he blames it on the objects durability and offers another attempt.
	ArmsDealer: A rude human individual who came from another dimension entirely. He got around in his life by selling illegal firearms and bullets to others. You might want to avoid messing with this shady guy on bad days.
	Mechanic: A woman with great technological knowledge who came from another dimension. She was transported here by an anomaly in space-time. She was found by the Cthulhu cult and thrown into the Dungeon to force her to use this �magic� she brought with her to aid their rituals.
	Steampunker: The steampunker seems to come from the same dimension as the Mechanic. She has a unique taste of inventions, where there is normally steel and wire, are instead cogs and steam. Despite being inferior to proper tech in terms of efficiency, it has been proven to run smoothly without issues ever.
	Cyborg: A group project that was built by the Mechanic and Steampunker during their time here. It was a great challenge with the limited technology they have here. The cyborg has an unusually well crafted soul system that grants him pre-coded emotions.
	Princess: Why are you like this..?
}
